{{!--
  Offline-first pattern decision ("19 §19.1's own "offline-first patterns" row) -- renders the
  already-registered `ADR` type (@forge/schemas' own registry) rather than a new module-owned schema:
  choosing a sync strategy/conflict-resolution/local-persistence approach for a mobile app is, honestly,
  an architectural decision with real options and real consequences, the identical "reuse an existing
  type, put structure in the body" choice modules/fm-service/module.yaml and
  modules/fm-data/module.yaml already make for their own OpenAPI/proto contracts and warehouse model --
  see agents/mobile.agent.yaml's own doc comment.

  Unlike modules/fm-service's own adr-*.md.hbs (a FRAMEWORK's own output_template, rendered against a
  scoring run's own execution data, per that file's own doc comment) this is a PLAIN module template --
  no framework produces this decision -- so it renders against 19 §19.2's own real `TemplateContext`
  shape (project/artifact/inputs/style/now/forge), matching modules/fm-web's/fm-data's own established
  convention for a template that is not a framework's own output_template. `framework: none` below is a
  real, honest literal (adrSchema's own `framework` field is `z.string().min(1)`, not optional) --
  stating plainly that no framework produced this decision, not fabricating an owner that does not
  exist.

  `created`/`updated`/`date` render `{{{artifact.created}}}`, a bare date (adrSchema's own
  `baseFrontMatterShape` types all three as `z.string().date()`), NOT the full ISO-8601 instant `now`
  carries -- the identical "artifact.created, not now" choice modules/fm-service's own openapi-contract/
  proto-contract templates already make, and the identical mistake (rendering `now` directly into a
  bare-date field) Q157/Q160 already document a critic round catching in the opposite direction.

  Only Handlebars built-in helpers are used (#each, #if) -- no custom helper is registered anywhere in
  this repository yet. Every triple-stash {{{ }}} is deliberate: this is a Markdown/YAML render target,
  not HTML, so a double-stash {{ }}'s default HTML-escaping would corrupt a YAML scalar containing an
  apostrophe or ampersand. Every array field's own {{#each}} carries an {{else}} branch rendering a
  literal "[]", the same reasoning adr-api-versioning.md.hbs's own doc comment already gives: an empty
  {{#each}} with no {{else}} renders nothing at all, leaving the YAML key with no value (parses as null,
  not []) -- adrSchema's own array fields reject null.

  This file is listed in .prettierignore (the identical "YAML front matter plus Handlebars block
  helpers" corruption class already documented there for packages/templates/templates/adr-*.md.hbs and
  modules/fm-web's/fm-service's/fm-data's own *.md.hbs templates -- prettier's markdown formatter
  reflows prose and merges distinct YAML keys onto one line, silently corrupting both the YAML and the
  template's own control flow).
--}}
